  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant to UNFPA TEENS Project 2021 grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project employs iterative design approaches and new technologies in the support to safe spaces for vulnerable women and adolescent girls. The programme strategy will provide safe spaces of engagement for women and adolescent girls that for the first time in Malawi employs new technologies as network and information platforms and a significant scaling up strategy for safe spaces. .  The programme will target a total population of indirect beneficiaries of  44,675 girls and young women and boys and men between 15-24 years in Lilongwe a semi-urban area. The direct target population and primary beneficiaries of the programme are the 3,100 adolescent girls and women between 15-24 years.</narrative>
  </description>
